2. SUPABASE DATABASE

Status: PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED

The initial migration defines users, games, user_games, achievements, user_achievements, game_reviews, and sync_logs.

Users:
- UUID primary key
- Unique optional text steam_id
- Username, display name, avatar, timestamps

Games:
- UUID primary key
- Required unique positive Steam App ID
- Title and optional metadata/artwork/developer/publisher/release fields
- Created/updated timestamps

User games:
- User and game foreign keys
- Playtime in minutes
- Status: Currently Playing, Completed, Backlog, or Abandoned
- Date added and last played timestamps
- Unique user/game pair

Achievements:
- Game relationship, Steam achievement API name, title, description, icon, hidden flag
- Unique game/achievement API name pair

User achievements:
- User and achievement relationships
- Unlock state and unlocked timestamp
- Unique user/achievement pair
- Unlocked rows require unlocked_at

Game reviews:
- User and game relationships
- Rating from 1 through 10
- Optional review text
- Unique user/game pair

Sync logs:
- User relationship
- Pending, Running, Succeeded, or Failed status
- Games synced count and error message
- Start/completion timestamps

Indexes:
- User/game ownership, status, achievement ownership, game review lookup, and sync-log ordering.

Triggers:
- Updated-at triggers exist for users, games, user_games, user_achievements, and game_reviews.

RLS:
- Enabled on all application tables.
- Shared games and achievements are public-read.
- Private rows are intended to match auth.uid() to application UUIDs.
- Review and sync-log policies exist.

Missing or unconfirmed:
- No confirmed migration application to local or remote Supabase.
- No Steam SteamID/user identity mapping flow.
- public.users.id is not documented as being automatically linked to auth.uid().
- No wishlist table or wishlist synchronization fields.
- No historical playtime record table if future activity charts require real history.
- No synchronization source/version fields, Steam API cache fields, or sync result detail structure.
- No Steam token fields for authenticated APIs, if Steam access requires them.

Exact file:
- supabase/migrations/20261107000000_initial_gamevault_schema.sql

Schema readiness:
The schema can support libraries, metadata, achievements, reviews, and basic sync logs, but it does not yet support a verified Steam-to-Supabase identity or Steam wishlist synchronization.

