5. SECURITY FINDINGS

| # | Severity | File | Lines | Vulnerability | Confidence |
|---|----------|------|-------|---------------|------------|
| 1 | HIGH | server/controllers/authController.js; server/routes/authRoutes.js | 5-8; authRoutes.js:6 | Development authentication remains available whenever NODE_ENV is not exactly production. On a misconfigured deployment it can provide a fixed authenticated development user. | 9/10 |
| 2 | MEDIUM | server/config/session.js | 10-44 | Sessions are process-local and disappear or split across server restarts and multiple instances; no persistent/shared session store exists. | 8/10 |
| 3 | MEDIUM | server/app.js | 8-10; server/routes/authRoutes.js | No Steam callback/OpenID state validation route exists, and protected backend routes do not currently use requireAuth. | 8/10 |
| 4 | MEDIUM | supabase/migrations/20261107000000_initial_gamevault_schema.sql | 121-177 | RLS policies assume Supabase auth.uid(), while the Express development session identity is unrelated to Supabase Auth. Private data access is not securely wired yet. | 8/10 |
| 5 | LOW | server/app.js | 8-10; server/package.json | No security headers or rate limiting middleware are configured, and all authentication/browser entry-point hardening remains unimplemented. | 7/10 |

Additional security observations:
- Development cookies are HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax; secure is enabled only in production.
- Session IDs use random 32-byte tokens and HMAC-SHA256 signatures.
- Session validation uses timing-safe signature comparison.
- The logout route clears the cookie after removing the server session.
- Session values are not persisted server-side or signed against a deployment shared secret in multi-instance deployments.
- No session renewal or idle timeout cleanup is implemented.
- The fixed development identity is not a real Steam or Supabase user.

SECRETS AUDIT

No Steam secret, Supabase service-role key, or Supabase private key is visible in the inspected source.

The browser Supabase environment file contains a Supabase URL and publishable/anon key:
- client/.env
- client/src/lib/supabase.js

These browser-visible values should remain publishable. The file is ignored by the root .gitignore, but its contents should not be committed accidentally.

Missing server environment documentation should include future Supabase service variables and Steam credentials, with secrets kept server-side only.

