The service-role key must never be placed in VITE_* variables or frontend code.

RECOMMENDED FIXES BEFORE STEAM INTEGRATION

1. Choose the identity architecture before implementation.
   - Supabase Auth user plus Steam identity mapping, or
   - Express Steam OpenID session plus an application user mapping and server-only Supabase access.

2. Disable development authentication by default outside an explicit local development mode.

3. Add a real Steam OpenID callback route, return-to validation, state validation, and verified Steam ID extraction.

4. Define the mapping between public.users.id, Steam ID, Supabase auth.uid(), and Express sessions.

5. Add server-only Supabase configuration and use service access only behind authenticated Express routes, or issue a Supabase-compatible identity if direct browser access is retained.

6. Replace the in-memory session store before production deployment with a shared persistent store.

7. Add secure production cookie settings and session rotation, expiration/cleanup, CSRF protections, and callback replay protection.

8. Add wishlist schema support if wishlist synchronization is required.

9. Add synchronization metadata and error handling before code reads Steam-owned/private data.

10. Protect all backend synchronization routes with requireAuth and derive the Steam ID from the verified session, never from client-provided user/game identifiers.


