Implementation status: completed for the requested backend identity foundation.

FILES CREATED

- server/config/supabase.js
  Reusable lazy Supabase server client. Reads SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY only from server environment variables. Configures the client without browser session persistence.

- server/test/auth.test.js
  Backend tests for production blocking, explicit development configuration, development login, session restoration, and HttpOnly cookies.

FILES MODIFIED

- server/controllers/authController.js
  Development login now requires both NODE_ENV=development and ENABLE_DEVELOPMENT_AUTH=true. Development sessions include explicit gameVaultUserId and steamId fields set to null. Cookie options now include HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure configuration, and Path=/.

- server/config/session.js
  No implementation change was required. Its current behavior remains an in-memory development session store with HMAC-signed tokens and a 24-hour TTL.

- server/.env.example
  Added SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE, ENABLE_DEVELOPMENT_AUTH, SUPABASE_URL, and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY placeholders.

